# Kebu — Task Workflow

**Master contract:** `docs/product/KEBU-MASTER-ENGINEERING-INSTRUCTION.md` · **Product Architect:** `docs/product/KEBU-PRODUCT-ARCHITECT-PHASE.md` · `kebu-master-engineering.mdc`

For every assigned feature (never invent scope):

## A0. Product Architect (new major surfaces)

If the slice introduces a **new product category or major surface**, output full blueprint **before code** — IA, screens, journeys, data, states, backend, tests. See `kebu-product-architect.mdc`.

## A. Inspect first (no edits)

UI, components, state, APIs, services, DB, migrations, authn/authz, jobs, providers, tests, deploy config.

## B. Report before coding

Exists · missing · broken · disconnected · files to change · DB changes · risks · end-to-end flow · acceptance criteria.

## C. One vertical slice

User action → FE validation → authenticated request → authorization → business logic → **Supabase** → DB → response → UI → **refresh verification**.

**If a dependency slice is broken:** **STOP** — repair dependency end-to-end before continuing. **Do not** build new functionality on broken functionality.

## D–E. Test and manually verify

Unit + integration + E2E (critical) · typecheck · lint · production build · valid/invalid/logged-out/wrong-user/network/duplicate/refresh/mobile/DB/logs.

## F. Adversarial self-audit (mandatory before next slice)

Frontend-only · disconnected API · missing writes · fake success · missing authz · cross-user leaks · RLS gaps · races · duplicate requests · broken refresh · weak tests · skipped requirements · competitor-clone UI without Kebu differentiation. **Trace every user action frontend → Supabase → frontend.** Repair before claiming progress or starting the next slice.

**Assigned audit prompt:** *“Audit Slice N as an adversarial senior engineer. Fix everything you find. Do not move to Slice N+1.”*

**Bugs:** discover → reproduce → root-cause fix → regression test when practical. **Never hide errors** to make UI look functional. Do not ignore. Do not claim zero bugs. **Stop and repair broken dependencies** before stacking new work.

## G. Completion report

Implemented · files · migrations · data flow · security · tests + commands + results · build · manual · DB · limitations · unfinished requirements.

When asked to audit only: **read-only**; severity-ranked defects; no code changes until assigned repair.
